### Crypto Tracker API — manual requests (Stage 0: base setup, Stage 2: api-rest,
### Stage 3: auth-firebase)
### Use with the REST Client extension (VS Code) or any compatible .http runner.
### Run `npm run dev` first, then send requests against http://localhost:3000.
### Stage 2 requires a seeded catalog (`npm run seed:coins`) and at least one
### `poll-prices` run (`npm run job:poll-prices` or `npm run dev:worker`) for
### non-empty responses.
### Stage 3 requests need a Firebase ID token: get one with
### `npm run auth:create-test-user -- --email ... --password ...` followed by
### `npm run --silent auth:token -- --email ... --password ...` (see the
### README's "Firebase Auth: development scripts and the Auth emulator"
### section), then replace `<your-id-token>` below with it. The admin requests
### additionally need that user promoted with
### `npm run user:set-role -- --email ... --role admin` (or created with
### `auth:create-test-user --admin` directly). `ADMIN_API_KEY`/`X-Admin-Key`
### no longer exist.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@idToken = <your-id-token>
@adminIdToken = <your-admin-id-token>

### Liveness: never touches the database.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Readiness: checks Mongo connectivity (200 when up, 503 when down).
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Request id is echoed back when supplied by the client.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: manual-test-123

### Unknown route -> 404 NOT_FOUND with the global error format.
GET {{baseUrl}}/no-existe

### Malformed JSON body -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR ("JSON inválido").
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{"invalid": json}

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): coin read endpoints
### ============================================================

### List coins: default page/limit, sorted by market cap descending.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins

### List coins with explicit pagination, sort and order.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?page=1&limit=10&sort=change24h&order=asc

### List coins matching a name/symbol prefix (case-insensitive).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?q=bit

### Unknown query param -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (E2-4).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins?foo=1

### Coin detail.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin

### Unknown coin -> 404 NOT_FOUND.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/no-existe

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): price history
### ============================================================

### Raw points over a short window (interval auto-selected as "raw").
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?from=2026-09-22T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-22T06:00:00Z

### Explicit interval=raw.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=raw&from=2026-09-22T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-22T06:00:00Z

### Bucketed OHLC candles (interval=1h) over 7 days, with a 3-bucket SMA.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=1h&from=2026-09-16T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z&sma=3

### Bucketed OHLC candles (interval=1d) over 90 days.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=1d&from=2026-06-25T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z

### raw over a range exceeding the 7-day cap -> 400 suggesting interval=1h (E2-8).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/history?interval=raw&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): price stats
### ============================================================

### Default range (24h).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats

### 7-day range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats?range=7d

### 90-day range (the range RNF-2.1 sets a p95 < 200ms budget for).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coins/bitcoin/stats?range=90d

### ============================================================
### Stage 2 (api-rest): status
### ============================================================

### Public worker-health summary — no admin key required.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/status

### ============================================================
### Stage 3 (auth-firebase): the authenticated user's own profile
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED (E3-1).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me

### With a valid token: provisions the profile on first call, then returns it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Update the editable field.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"displayName": "Nico"}

### `role`/`email` are not editable -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (E3-8).
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"role": "admin"}

### Deletes this application's own profile only (204); the Firebase account
### survives and re-provisions an empty profile on the next authenticated call.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### ============================================================
### Stage 2/3: admin job-runs (requireAuth + requireRole('admin'))
### ============================================================

### Without a token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED (E3-10; the old X-Admin-Key header,
### if sent instead, is simply ignored and still yields 401).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs

### Authenticated but not an admin -> 403 FORBIDDEN (E3-9).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs
Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}

### Paginated list, filtered by status, with an admin token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs?status=success,partial&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Filtered by jobName and a startedAt range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs?jobName=poll-prices&from=2026-09-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-23T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Job run detail by id (replace with a real _id from the list above).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs/651f1c2e8b1e2a0012a3b456
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}

### Malformed id -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/job-runs/not-an-object-id
Authorization: Bearer {{adminIdToken}}
